file.content:
# Carousel Interface: Carousel Component

**Project:** Turn-Centric Cognitive Interface
**Component:** Central Carousel
**Status:** Draft
**Last Updated:** December 2025

---

## 1. Purpose

The Carousel is the central component of the interface. It transforms conversation from a scrolling log into a **navigable timeline of turn cards**. Each card represents one complete exchange: user message + AI response.

---

## 2. Core Concepts

### 2.1 The Turn Card

A **Turn** is the atomic unit:

```
Turn = User Message + AI Response
```

Each turn becomes a **Card** - a manipulable object that can be:
- Navigated to
- Selected
- Acted upon
- Transformed into artifacts
- Collapsed or expanded
- Tagged and organized

### 2.2 The Carousel Strip

Cards are arranged in a **horizontal strip**:

```
◀ ── [Card 1] ── [Card 2] ── [Card 3*] ── [Card 4] ── [Card 5] ── ▶
                              (selected)
```

The strip is:
- Horizontally scrollable
- Keyboard navigable
- Touch/swipe enabled
- Momentum-based scrolling

---

## 3. Card Anatomy

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  Card Title (auto or user-edited)              [#tag]  │  │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                              │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  USER                                                  │  │
│  │  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────    │  │
│  │  User's message content goes here. Can be multiple     │  │
│  │  lines and includes any formatting from the original   │  │
│  │  input.                                                │  │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                              │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  AI                                           ▼ scroll │  │
│  │  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────    │  │
│  │  AI response content. This section is independently    │  │
│  │  scrollable when content exceeds the card's max        │  │
│  │  height. Markdown rendering is supported including:    │  │
│  │                                                        │  │
│  │  - Code blocks with syntax highlighting                │  │
│  │  - Lists and tables                                    │  │
│  │  - Headers and formatting                              │  │
│  │                                                        │  │
│  │  The card maintains its position in the carousel       │  │
│  │  while internal content scrolls.                       │  │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                              │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  [Collapse] [Branch] [Promote]     12:34 PM · Turn 3   │  │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 3.1 Card Sections

| Section | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| **Title Bar** | Auto-generated summary, user-editable, optional tags |
| **User Section** | Original user input, non-scrollable |
| **AI Section** | AI response, independently scrollable |
| **Footer** | Local actions, timestamp, turn number |

---

## 4. Card States

### 4.1 Visual States

| State | Appearance | Trigger |
|-------|------------|---------|
| **Default** | Standard glass card | No interaction |
| **Hover** | Elevated shadow, slight lift | Mouse over |
| **Selected** | Focus ring, elevated | Click or keyboard |
| **Collapsed** | Minimal height, title only | User action |
| **Loading** | Skeleton + spinner | Awaiting AI response |
| **Error** | Error border, retry option | Request failed |

### 4.2 State Transitions

```typescript
type CardState =
  | "default"
  | "hover"
  | "selected"
  | "collapsed"
  | "loading"
  | "error";

// Framer Motion variants
const cardVariants = {
  default: {
    scale: 1,
    y: 0,
    boxShadow: "var(--shadow-card)",
  },
  hover: {
    scale: 1.01,
    y: -2,
    boxShadow: "var(--shadow-elevated)",
  },
  selected: {
    scale: 1,
    y: 0,
    boxShadow: "0 0 0 2px var(--accent-focus), var(--shadow-elevated)",
  },
  collapsed: {
    scale: 1,
    y: 0,
  },
};
```

---

## 5. Card Data Model

```typescript
interface TurnCard {
  id: string;                    // Unique identifier
  index: number;                 // Position in carousel (0-based)

  // Content
  title: string;                 // Auto-generated or user-edited
  titleEdited: boolean;          // Track if user changed title
  userContent: string;           // User's message (markdown)
  aiContent: string;             // AI's response (markdown)

  // State
  state: CardState;
  collapsed: boolean;

  // Metadata
  tags: string[];
  timestamp: string;             // ISO 8601
  branchId?: string;             // If part of a branch
  promotedFrom?: string;         // If promoted from side thread

  // Computed
  wordCount: number;
  hasCode: boolean;              // Contains code blocks
  hasTables: boolean;            // Contains tables
}
```

---

## 6. Carousel Container

### 6.1 Layout Structure

```typescript
interface CarouselProps {
  cards: TurnCard[];
  selectedIndex: number;
  onSelectCard: (index: number) => void;
  onCardAction: (cardId: string, action: CardAction) => void;
}
```

### 6.2 CSS Layout

```css
.carousel-container {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  height: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
  padding: var(--space-8) 0;
}

.carousel-track {
  display: flex;
  gap: var(--card-gap);
  padding: 0 calc(50% - var(--card-width) / 2);
  scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
  overflow-x: auto;
  scrollbar-width: none;
}

.carousel-track::-webkit-scrollbar {
  display: none;
}

.carousel-card {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  width: var(--card-width);
  min-height: var(--card-min-height);
  max-height: var(--card-max-height);
  scroll-snap-align: center;
}
```

---

## 7. Navigation

### 7.1 Navigation Methods

| Method | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| **Click** | Select card, scroll to center |
| **Arrow keys** | Move selection left/right |
| **Swipe** | Momentum scroll, snap to nearest |
| **Scroll wheel** | Horizontal scroll (with shift) |
| **Home/End** | Jump to first/last card |
| **Number keys** | Jump to card N (1-9) |

### 7.2 Scroll Behavior

```typescript
const scrollToCard = (index: number) => {
  const card = cards[index];
  if (!card) return;

  // Smooth scroll with spring animation
  animate(scrollX, targetPosition, {
    type: "spring",
    stiffness: 300,
    damping: 30,
  });
};
```

### 7.3 Keyboard Handling

```typescript
const handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
  switch (e.key) {
    case "ArrowLeft":
      selectCard(Math.max(0, selectedIndex - 1));
      break;
    case "ArrowRight":
      selectCard(Math.min(cards.length - 1, selectedIndex + 1));
      break;
    case "Home":
      selectCard(0);
      break;
    case "End":
      selectCard(cards.length - 1);
      break;
    case "Enter":
      openCardActions();
      break;
    case "Escape":
      deselectCard();
      break;
  }
};
```

---

## 8. Card Actions

Actions available on each card (also surfaced in East Quadrant):

### 8.1 Action Types

```typescript
type CardAction =
  | { type: "collapse" }
  | { type: "expand" }
  | { type: "branch" }
  | { type: "promote"; target: "main" | "thread" }
  | { type: "convert"; to: ArtifactType }
  | { type: "summarize" }
  | { type: "tag"; tag: string }
  | { type: "untag"; tag: string }
  | { type: "editTitle"; title: string }
  | { type: "delete" }
  | { type: "copy"; section: "user" | "ai" | "both" }
  | { type: "exportCode" };

type ArtifactType =
  | "task"
  | "document"
  | "github-issue"
  | "whitepaper-seed"
  | "summary";
```

### 8.2 Action Availability

| Action | When Available |
|--------|----------------|
| Collapse/Expand | Always |
| Branch | Main carousel only |
| Promote | Side thread cards only |
| Convert | Card has substantive content |
| Summarize | AI content > 200 words |
| Tag | Always |
| Delete | Not loading, not only card |
| Export Code | Card contains code blocks |

---

## 9. Title Generation

### 9.1 Auto-Generation Rules

Titles are auto-generated from content:

1. If user message is a question, use first 50 chars
2. If user message is a command, summarize the intent
3. If AI response has a clear topic, extract it
4. Fallback: "Turn {n}"

```typescript
const generateTitle = (card: TurnCard): string => {
  const userText = card.userContent.trim();

  // Question detection
  if (userText.endsWith("?")) {
    return truncate(userText, 50);
  }

  // Command detection
  const commands = ["create", "write", "fix", "explain", "help"];
  for (const cmd of commands) {
    if (userText.toLowerCase().startsWith(cmd)) {
      return truncate(userText, 50);
    }
  }

  // Extract from AI response
  const firstLine = card.aiContent.split("\n")[0];
  if (firstLine.startsWith("#")) {
    return firstLine.replace(/^#+\s*/, "").slice(0, 50);
  }

  return `Turn ${card.index + 1}`;
};
```

### 9.2 User Editing

Double-click title to edit. Changes persist and set `titleEdited: true`.

---

## 10. Collapsed State

When collapsed, card shows only:

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Card Title                                    [Expand] [#]  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Collapsed cards:
- Take minimal horizontal space
- Remain navigable
- Show expand affordance on hover
- Display tag indicators

---

## 11. Loading State

When awaiting AI response:

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  New Conversation                                      │  │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                              │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  USER                                                  │  │
│  │  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────    │  │
│  │  User's message that was just sent...                  │  │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                              │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  AI                                                    │  │
│  │  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────    │  │
│  │  ████████████████████████                              │  │
│  │  ████████████████████                                  │  │
│  │  ██████████████████████████                            │  │
│  │                          ◐ (spinner)                   │  │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 12. Responsive Behavior

### 12.1 Desktop (1024px+)

- Full carousel with multiple visible cards
- Selected card centered
- Adjacent cards visible on sides

### 12.2 Tablet (768px - 1023px)

- Narrower cards (400px)
- Fewer visible adjacent cards
- Same interaction model

### 12.3 Mobile (< 768px)

- Full-width cards
- Single card visible at a time
- Swipe to navigate
- Bottom sheet for actions

---

## 13. Performance Considerations

### 13.1 Virtualization

For conversations with many turns:

```typescript
// Only render cards within viewport + buffer
const visibleRange = {
  start: Math.max(0, selectedIndex - 3),
  end: Math.min(cards.length - 1, selectedIndex + 3),
};

const visibleCards = cards.slice(visibleRange.start, visibleRange.end + 1);
```

### 13.2 Content Truncation

Long AI responses:
- Render first 5000 characters initially
- Load more on scroll within card
- Never block carousel navigation

### 13.3 Image Handling

- Lazy load images in card content
- Placeholder during load
- Max dimensions to prevent layout shift

---

## 14. Component API

```typescript
// Main carousel component
export const Carousel: React.FC<{
  cards: TurnCard[];
  selectedIndex: number;
  onSelect: (index: number) => void;
  onAction: (cardId: string, action: CardAction) => void;
}>;

// Individual card component
export const Card: React.FC<{
  card: TurnCard;
  isSelected: boolean;
  onSelect: () => void;
  onAction: (action: CardAction) => void;
}>;

// Card content renderer
export const CardContent: React.FC<{
