---

## 7. WebSocket Protocol

### 7.1 Connection

```
ws://localhost:3001/ws
```

No auth for MVP. Connection is per-browser-tab.

### 7.2 Message Types

```typescript
// Client → Server
type ClientMessage =
  | { type: "SUBSCRIBE"; sessionId: string }
  | { type: "UNSUBSCRIBE"; sessionId: string }
  | { type: "PING" };

// Server → Client
type ServerMessage =
  | { type: "PONG" }
  | { type: "SUBSCRIBED"; sessionId: string }
  | { type: "STREAM_START"; cardId: string }
  | { type: "STREAM_CHUNK"; cardId: string; content: string; index: number }
  | { type: "STREAM_END"; cardId: string; card: TurnCard }
  | { type: "STREAM_ERROR"; cardId: string; error: string }
  | { type: "SESSION_UPDATED"; session: Partial<Session> };
```

### 7.3 Streaming Flow

```
Client                          Server                          OpenAI
   │                               │                               │
   │  POST /messages               │                               │
   │  { content: "..." }           │                               │
   │ ─────────────────────────────▶│                               │
   │                               │  stream: true                 │
   │                               │ ─────────────────────────────▶│
   │  { cardId, status }           │                               │
   │ ◀─────────────────────────────│                               │
   │                               │                               │
   │  WS: STREAM_START             │  chunk                        │
   │ ◀─────────────────────────────│◀─────────────────────────────│
   │                               │                               │
   │  WS: STREAM_CHUNK             │  chunk                        │
   │ ◀─────────────────────────────│◀─────────────────────────────│
   │                               │                               │
   │  WS: STREAM_CHUNK             │  chunk                        │
   │ ◀─────────────────────────────│◀─────────────────────────────│
   │                               │                               │
   │  WS: STREAM_END               │  done                         │
   │ ◀─────────────────────────────│◀─────────────────────────────│
   │                               │                               │
   │                               │  (save to session file)       │
   │                               │                               │
```

---

## 8. Context Building

### 8.1 System Prompt Construction

Uses the Context Assembler (Section 4.3) to fetch documents from Artifact Engine:

```typescript
const buildSystemPrompt = async (
  persona: Persona,
  scope: ContextScope,
  distillation?: SessionDistillation
): Promise<string> => {
  // 1. Base persona prompt
  let prompt = persona.systemPrompt;

  // 2. Fetch documents from Artifact Engine via Context Assembler
  const assembled = await assembleContext(scope);

  prompt += `\n\n## Reference Documents\n\n`;
  prompt += `You have access to the following documents. Reference them when answering questions.\n\n`;
  prompt += assembled.contextString;

  // 3. Add distillation context (if exists)
  if (distillation) {
    prompt += `\n\n## Session Context\n\n`;
    prompt += `Summary so far: ${distillation.summary}\n\n`;
    prompt += `Key insights explored:\n`;
    distillation.keyInsights.forEach(i => prompt += `- ${i}\n`);
  }

  return prompt;
};
```

### 8.2 Token Budget (Future V2)

For smart selection in V2:

```typescript
interface TokenBudget {
  systemPrompt: number;      // ~500 tokens
  documents: number;         // ~100k tokens available
  conversation: number;      // ~8k tokens for history
  response: number;          // ~4k tokens reserved
}

// V2: Select documents per-turn based on query
const selectRelevantDocs = async (
  query: string,
  scope: ContextScope,
  budget: number
): Promise<ArtifactSearchResult[]> => {
  // Use Artifact Engine search with keywords extracted from query
  const keywords = extractKeywords(query);
  const results = await artifactClient.search({
    domain: "whitepapers",
    keywords,
  });

  // Filter to stay within token budget
  return filterByTokenBudget(results, budget);
};
```

---

## 9. Distillation Service

### 9.1 Purpose

Periodically summarize the session to:
- Maintain coherence in long sessions
- Provide exportable notes
- Reduce context window usage

### 9.2 Trigger

```typescript
const shouldDistill = (session: Session): boolean => {
  const lastDistill = session.distillation?.turnCount ?? 0;
  const currentTurns = session.cards.length;

  // Distill every 5 turns
  return currentTurns - lastDistill >= 5;
};
```

### 9.3 Distillation Prompt

```typescript
const distillSession = async (session: Session): Promise<SessionDistillation> => {
  const conversationText = session.cards
    .map(c => `User: ${c.userContent}\nAssistant: ${c.aiContent}`)
    .join('\n\n---\n\n');

  const response = await openai.chat.completions.create({
    model: "gpt-4",
    messages: [
      {
        role: "system",
        content: `Analyze this conversation and provide:
1. A 2-3 sentence summary of what was discussed
2. Key insights or conclusions (bullet points)
3. Main questions that were explored (bullet points)

Be concise. This will be used as context for continuing the conversation.`
      },
      {
        role: "user",
        content: conversationText
      }
    ],
    response_format: { type: "json_object" }
  });

  return JSON.parse(response.choices[0].message.content);
};
```

### 9.4 MVP Stub

For MVP, distillation is optional. Stub it:

```typescript
// services/distillation.ts
export const distillSession = async (session: Session): Promise<SessionDistillation | null> => {
  // MVP: return null, implement later
  return null;
};
```

---

## 10. OpenAI Integration

### 10.1 Client Setup

```typescript
// services/openai.ts
import OpenAI from "openai";
import { config } from "../config";

export const openai = new OpenAI({
  apiKey: config.openaiApiKey,
});
```

### 10.2 Streaming Handler

```typescript
export const streamCompletion = async (
  messages: ChatMessage[],
  onChunk: (content: string, index: number) => void,
  onComplete: (fullContent: string) => void,
  onError: (error: Error) => void
): Promise<void> => {
  try {
    const stream = await openai.chat.completions.create({
      model: config.model,  // "gpt-4" or "gpt-4-turbo"
      messages,
      stream: true,
    });

    let fullContent = "";
    let index = 0;

    for await (const chunk of stream) {
      const content = chunk.choices[0]?.delta?.content || "";
      if (content) {
        fullContent += content;
        onChunk(content, index++);
      }
    }

    onComplete(fullContent);
  } catch (error) {
    onError(error as Error);
  }
};
```

### 10.3 Message Building

```typescript
export const buildMessages = (
  systemPrompt: string,
  cards: TurnCard[],
  newUserMessage: string
): ChatMessage[] => {
  const messages: ChatMessage[] = [
    { role: "system", content: systemPrompt }
  ];

  // Add conversation history
  for (const card of cards) {
    messages.push({ role: "user", content: card.userContent });
    messages.push({ role: "assistant", content: card.aiContent });
  }

  // Add new message
  messages.push({ role: "user", content: newUserMessage });

  return messages;
};
```

