# Turnstile: Backend Architecture

**Project:** Turnstile
**Component:** Backend Server
**Status:** Draft
**Last Updated:** December 2025

---

## 1. Design Philosophy

This is not a general-purpose chat backend. It's an **interactive document companion** - a focused exploration interface for a bounded corpus.

| Principle | Implementation |
|-----------|----------------|
| **Corpus is fixed** | Whitepapers/documents are versioned but stable |
| **Sessions are ephemeral** | Explore, export notes, then gone |
| **No cross-session memory** | Fresh start each time, like rereading a book |
| **JSON everywhere** | File-based storage, no database for MVP |
| **Streaming responses** | Real-time token delivery via WebSocket |
| **Artifact Engine integration** | Documents stored/retrieved via existing infrastructure |

---

## 2. Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        Frontend                              │
│                   (React + WebSocket)                        │
└─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   Turnstile Backend                          │
│              (Thin orchestration layer)                      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Routes:                                                     │
│  ├─ /sessions      Session CRUD (JSON files)                │
│  ├─ /messages      OpenAI proxy + streaming                 │
│  ├─ /context       Scope listing + assembly                 │
│  └─ /personas      List available personas                  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Services:                                                   │
│  ├─ Context Assembler    Builds LLM context from docs       │
│  └─ Artifact Client      HTTP calls to Artifact Engine      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  WebSocket:                                                  │
│  └─ Stream chunks, state updates                            │
└─────────────┬─────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┘
              │                     │
              ▼                     ▼
┌───────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────┐
│   Artifact Engine     │   │     OpenAI API      │
│   (localhost:3002)    │   │                     │
├───────────────────────┤   └─────────────────────┘
│  GET  /artifact/<id>/content
│  POST /artifact/search
│  GET  /registry/locations
└───────────────────────┘
              │
              ▼
┌───────────────────────┐
│  artifacts/           │
│    whitepapers/       │
│      sdb-framework/   │
│      implementation/  │
└───────────────────────┘
```

**Key insight:** Turnstile backend is a thin orchestration layer. Document storage, validation, and retrieval are delegated to Artifact Engine. Turnstile just assembles context and proxies to OpenAI.

---

## 3. Directory Structure

```
turnstile-backend/
├── src/
│   ├── server.ts              # Express + WebSocket setup
│   ├── config.ts              # Environment variables
│   ├── routes/
│   │   ├── sessions.ts        # Session CRUD
│   │   ├── messages.ts        # OpenAI streaming proxy
│   │   ├── context.ts         # Scope listing (wraps Artifact Engine)
│   │   └── personas.ts        # Persona listing
│   ├── services/
│   │   ├── openai.ts          # OpenAI client wrapper
│   │   ├── artifact-client.ts # HTTP client for Artifact Engine
│   │   ├── context-assembler.ts # Builds LLM context from docs
│   │   └── distillation.ts    # Session summarization (v1 stub)
│   ├── storage/
│   │   └── sessions.ts        # Session JSON file operations
│   └── types/
│       └── index.ts           # Shared TypeScript interfaces
├── data/
│   ├── personas/
│   │   └── personas.json      # Hardcoded personas
│   └── sessions/
│       └── *.json             # One file per session
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
└── .env

# Documents live in Artifact Engine, not here:
# artifact-engine/
#   artifacts/
#     whitepapers/
#       sdb-framework/
#         software_defined_business.md
#         flow_defined_work.md
#       implementation/
#         declarative_cad.md
#         acoustic_intelligence.md
```

---

## 4. Artifact Engine Integration

### 4.1 Artifact Client

A simple HTTP client that wraps Artifact Engine's API:

```typescript
// services/artifact-client.ts
import { config } from "../config";

const ARTIFACT_ENGINE_URL = config.artifactEngineUrl; // http://localhost:3002

export const artifactClient = {
  // Get registry to discover available domains/locations
  async getLocations(): Promise<LocationRegistry> {
    const res = await fetch(`${ARTIFACT_ENGINE_URL}/registry/locations`);
    const data = await res.json();
    // Registry returns { locations: { "prefix": {...}, ... } }
    return data.locations;
  },

  // Search for documents by domain/location
  // Adapts our query shape to Artifact Engine's API
  async search(query: ArtifactSearchQuery): Promise<ArtifactSearchResult[]> {
    // Artifact Engine expects plural arrays for domains/locations
    const engineQuery: ArtifactEngineSearchQuery = {
      domains: query.domain ? [query.domain] : undefined,
      locations: query.location ? [query.location] : undefined,
      keywords: query.keywords,
      tags: query.tags,
      topics: query.topics,
      limit: query.limit,
      offset: query.offset,
    };

    const res = await fetch(`${ARTIFACT_ENGINE_URL}/artifact/search`, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify(engineQuery),
    });
    const data = await res.json();
    // Artifact Engine returns { results: [...], elimination_trace: {...} }
    return data.results;
  },

  // Get document content by ID
  async getContent(artifactId: string): Promise<string> {
    const res = await fetch(`${ARTIFACT_ENGINE_URL}/artifact/${artifactId}/content`);
    return res.text();
  },

  // Get document metadata
  async getMetadata(artifactId: string): Promise<ArtifactMetadata> {
    const res = await fetch(`${ARTIFACT_ENGINE_URL}/artifact/${artifactId}`);
    return res.json();
  },
};

// Turnstile's query interface (convenience layer)
interface ArtifactSearchQuery {
  domain?: string;           // e.g., "whitepapers" - wrapped to array for engine
  location?: string;         // e.g., "whitepapers/sdb-framework" - wrapped to array
  keywords?: string[];       // filename token matching
  tags?: string[];           // inferred from registry
  topics?: string[];         // inferred from registry
  limit?: number;
  offset?: number;
}

// Artifact Engine's actual API shape
interface ArtifactEngineSearchQuery {
  domains?: string[];        // plural array
  locations?: string[];      // plural array (was "category" in earlier draft)
  keywords?: string[];
  tags?: string[];
  topics?: string[];
  limit?: number;
  offset?: number;
}

interface ArtifactSearchResult {
  artifact_id: string;       // matches engine's response
  path: string;
  filename: string;
  domain: string;
  location: string;          // was "category" - now matches engine
  tags: string[];
  topics: string[];
  tokens: string[];
}

interface ArtifactMetadata {
  artifact_id: string;
  path: string;
  filename: string;
  domain: string;
  location: string;
  tags: string[];
  topics: string[];
  tokens: string[];
  fields: Record<string, string>;
}

// Registry is keyed by location prefix
type LocationRegistry = Record<string, LocationEntry>;

interface LocationEntry {
  domain: string;
  tags: string[];
  topics: string[];
  allowed_extensions: string[];
  filename_rules?: {
    token_delimiters: string[];
    case: string;
    patterns: Array<{ name: string; regex: string }>;
  };
}
```

### 4.2 Scope Discovery

The West quadrant dropdown is populated from Artifact Engine's registry:

```typescript
// services/context-assembler.ts
export const getAvailableScopes = async (): Promise<ContextScope[]> => {
  const locations = await artifactClient.getLocations();

  // Find the whitepapers domain
  const whitepaperLocation = locations.find(l => l.prefix === "whitepapers");
  if (!whitepaperLocation) return [];

  const scopes: ContextScope[] = [
    { type: "all", label: "All Whitepapers" }
  ];

  // Add categories as groups
  for (const category of whitepaperLocation.categories || []) {
    scopes.push({
      type: "group",
      groupId: category.id,
      label: category.name,
    });
  }

  // Add individual documents
  const allDocs = await artifactClient.search({ domain: "whitepapers" });
  for (const doc of allDocs) {
    scopes.push({
      type: "document",
      documentId: doc.id,
      label: inferTitle(doc.filename),
    });
  }

  return scopes;
};

const inferTitle = (filename: string): string => {
  // software_defined_business.md → "Software Defined Business"
  return filename
    .replace(/\.md$/, "")
    .replace(/_/g, " ")
    .replace(/\b\w/g, c => c.toUpperCase());
};
```

### 4.3 Context Assembly

The "baby assembler" - fetches documents and concatenates them:

```typescript
// services/context-assembler.ts
export const assembleContext = async (scope: ContextScope): Promise<AssembledContext> => {
  let artifacts: ArtifactSearchResult[];

  switch (scope.type) {
    case "all":
      artifacts = await artifactClient.search({ domain: "whitepapers" });
      break;
    case "group":
      artifacts = await artifactClient.search({
        domain: "whitepapers",
        category: scope.groupId
      });
      break;
    case "document":
      artifacts = await artifactClient.search({
        domain: "whitepapers"
      }).then(all => all.filter(a => a.id === scope.documentId));
      break;
  }

  // Fetch content for each document
  const documents: AssembledDocument[] = await Promise.all(
    artifacts.map(async (artifact) => ({
      id: artifact.id,
      title: inferTitle(artifact.filename),
      content: await artifactClient.getContent(artifact.id),
    }))
  );

  // Build the context string
  const contextString = documents
    .map(doc => `### ${doc.title}\n\n${doc.content}`)
    .join("\n\n---\n\n");

  return {
    documents,
    contextString,
    tokenEstimate: Math.ceil(contextString.length / 4), // Rough estimate
  };
};

interface AssembledContext {
  documents: AssembledDocument[];
  contextString: string;
  tokenEstimate: number;
}

interface AssembledDocument {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  content: string;
}
```

---

## 5. Data Models

### 5.1 Persona

```typescript
interface Persona {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  description: string;
  systemPrompt: string;
  suggestedCorpora?: string[];  // Which corpora this persona works well with
}
```

### Example: `data/personas/personas.json`

```json
{
  "personas": [
    {
      "id": "guide",
      "name": "Document Guide",
      "description": "Helps navigate and understand the corpus",
      "systemPrompt": "You are a knowledgeable guide helping users explore and understand a collection of technical documents. Answer questions by referencing specific sections. Suggest related topics when relevant. Be concise but thorough."
    },
    {
      "id": "architect",
      "name": "Software Architect",
      "description": "Technical implementation focus",
      "systemPrompt": "You are a senior software architect. Help users understand technical concepts, design patterns, and implementation strategies from the documents. Provide concrete examples and code snippets when helpful."
    },
    {
      "id": "sdb-expert",
      "name": "SDB Expert",
      "description": "Software-Defined Business specialist",
      "systemPrompt": "You are an expert in Software-Defined Business methodology. Help users apply declarative, intent-driven patterns to their business processes. Reference the SDB framework documents and explain how concepts interconnect."
    }
  ]
}
```

### 5.2 Session

```typescript
interface Session {
  id: string;
  corpusId: string;
  contextScope: ContextScope;
  personaId: string;
  title: string;
  mode: SessionMode;
  cards: TurnCard[];
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;

  // Distillation (updated periodically)
  distillation?: SessionDistillation;
}

type SessionMode = "strict" | "creative" | "analytical" | "writing";

interface ContextScope {
  type: "all" | "group" | "documents";
  groupId?: string;            // If type === "group"
  documentIds?: string[];      // If type === "documents"
}

interface SessionDistillation {
  summary: string;
  keyInsights: string[];
  questionsExplored: string[];
  updatedAt: string;
  turnCount: number;           // Turns when last updated
}

interface TurnCard {
  id: string;
  index: number;
  title: string;
  titleEdited: boolean;
  userContent: string;
  aiContent: string;
  timestamp: string;
  collapsed: boolean;
  tags: string[];

  // Metadata
  wordCount: number;
  hasCode: boolean;
  documentsReferenced?: string[];  // Which docs were in context
}
```

