## 8. Context Building

### 8.1 System Prompt Construction

Uses the Context Assembler (Section 4.3) to fetch documents from Artifact Engine:

```typescript
const buildSystemPrompt = async (
  persona: Persona,
  scope: ContextScope,
  distillation?: SessionDistillation
): Promise<string> => {
  // 1. Base persona prompt
  let prompt = persona.systemPrompt;

  // 2. Fetch documents from Artifact Engine via Context Assembler
  const assembled = await assembleContext(scope);

  prompt += `\n\n## Reference Documents\n\n`;
  prompt += `You have access to the following documents. Reference them when answering questions.\n\n`;
  prompt += assembled.contextString;

  // 3. Add distillation context (if exists)
  if (distillation) {
    prompt += `\n\n## Session Context\n\n`;
    prompt += `Summary so far: ${distillation.summary}\n\n`;
    prompt += `Key insights explored:\n`;
    distillation.keyInsights.forEach(i => prompt += `- ${i}\n`);
  }

  return prompt;
};
```

### 8.2 Token Budget (Future V2)

For smart selection in V2:

```typescript
interface TokenBudget {
  systemPrompt: number;      // ~500 tokens
  documents: number;         // ~100k tokens available
  conversation: number;      // ~8k tokens for history
  response: number;          // ~4k tokens reserved
}

// V2: Select documents per-turn based on query
const selectRelevantDocs = async (
  query: string,
  scope: ContextScope,
  budget: number
): Promise<ArtifactSearchResult[]> => {
  // Use Artifact Engine search with keywords extracted from query
  const keywords = extractKeywords(query);
  const results = await artifactClient.search({
    domain: "whitepapers",
    keywords,
  });

  // Filter to stay within token budget
  return filterByTokenBudget(results, budget);
};
```

